    "function": "Catalyzes the hydrolysis of both intracellular and extracellular triacylglycerol (TAG). In vitro, can also hydrolyze p-nitrophenyl (pNP) esters with various chain lengths, including pNP-acetate (C2), pNP-butyrate (C4), pNP-caproate (C6), pNP-caprylate (C8), pNP-laurate (C12), pNP-myristate (C14), pNP-palmitate (C16) and pNP-stearate (C18). Also hydrolyzes monobutyrin, tributyrin and trioctanoin. Overexpression results in increase of virulence characterized by reduced survival of infected mouse and increased burden of bacilli in the lungs. Hydrolyzes internal or host-derived TAG depending on it",
